$ nexoctl mb --with-lock mem/vault
Bucket created successfully `mem/vault` (with Object Lock).

$ nexoctl mb mem/plain
Bucket created successfully `mem/plain`.

$ nexoctl stat mem/vault
Name        : vault
Date        : 2026-01-02 03:04:05 UTC
Type        : bucket
Versioning  : Enabled
Object Lock : Enabled
Anonymous   : private

$ nexoctl retention info mem/vault
`mem/vault` has Object Lock, without default retention.

$ nexoctl retention info mem/plain
`mem/plain` has no Object Lock (create the bucket with "nexoctl mb --with-lock").

$ nexoctl retention set --default --mode governance --validity 7d mem/vault
Default retention of `mem/vault`: GOVERNANCE for 7d.

$ nexoctl retention info --default mem/vault
`mem/vault` has Object Lock, default retention GOVERNANCE for 7d.

$ nexoctl retention set --default --mode governance --validity 7d mem/plain
! nexoctl: error: mem/plain: conflict: Object Lock can only be enabled at the creation of a bucket (InvalidBucketState) (Object Lock is enabled when the bucket is created: nexoctl mb --with-lock)
[exit 1]

$ nexoctl cp doc.txt draft.txt mem/vault/
`doc.txt` -> `mem/vault/doc.txt` (15B)
`draft.txt` -> `mem/vault/draft.txt` (6B)
Copied 2 objects (21B).

$ nexoctl retention info mem/vault/doc.txt
`mem/vault/doc.txt`: GOVERNANCE until 2026-01-09 03:04:05 UTC (in force).

$ nexoctl stat mem/vault/doc.txt
Name        : doc.txt
Date        : 2026-01-02 03:04:05 UTC
Size        : 15B (15 bytes)
Type        : file
ETag        : a71cbb8265bb341e45e2f37e33b1bb47
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Class       : STANDARD
VersionID   : v0001
Retention   : GOVERNANCE until 2026-01-09 03:04:05 UTC

$ nexoctl retention set --mode compliance --validity 1y mem/vault/doc.txt
Retention of `mem/vault/doc.txt`: COMPLIANCE until 2027-01-02 03:04:05 UTC.

$ nexoctl retention clear --bypass mem/vault/doc.txt
! nexoctl: error: mem/vault/doc.txt: access denied: a COMPLIANCE retention can only be extended
[exit 4]

$ nexoctl legalhold set mem/vault/draft.txt
Legal hold of `mem/vault/draft.txt`: ON.

$ nexoctl legalhold info -r mem/vault/
`mem/vault/doc.txt`: legal hold OFF.
`mem/vault/draft.txt`: legal hold ON.

$ nexoctl retention info -r --json mem/vault
{"status":"success","target":"mem/vault/doc.txt","key":"doc.txt","mode":"COMPLIANCE","retainUntil":"2027-01-02T03:04:05Z"}
{"status":"success","target":"mem/vault/draft.txt","key":"draft.txt","mode":"GOVERNANCE","retainUntil":"2026-01-09T03:04:05Z"}

$ nexoctl rm --versions mem/vault/draft.txt
! warning: failed to remove `mem/vault/draft.txt`: access denied: the version is under legal hold
! nexoctl: error: 1 of 1 removals failed: mem/vault/draft.txt: access denied: the version is under legal hold
[exit 4]

$ nexoctl rb --force mem/vault
! warning: `mem/vault/doc.txt` (version v0001) is protected: COMPLIANCE retention until 2027-01-02 03:04:05 UTC
! warning: `mem/vault/draft.txt` (version v0002) is protected: GOVERNANCE retention until 2026-01-09 03:04:05 UTC, legal hold
! nexoctl: error: mem/vault: 2 versions protected by Object Lock, nothing removed (release the legal holds, wait for the retentions or remove the GOVERNANCE ones with "rm --versions --bypass"): object locked
[exit 4]

$ nexoctl legalhold clear mem/vault/draft.txt
Legal hold of `mem/vault/draft.txt`: OFF.

$ nexoctl rm --versions mem/vault/draft.txt
! warning: failed to remove `mem/vault/draft.txt`: access denied: the version is protected by a GOVERNANCE retention
! nexoctl: error: 1 of 1 removals failed: mem/vault/draft.txt: access denied: the version is protected by a GOVERNANCE retention
[exit 4]

$ nexoctl rm --versions --bypass mem/vault/draft.txt
Removed `mem/vault/draft.txt` (version v0002).

$ nexoctl ls --versions --recursive mem/vault
[2026-01-02 03:04:05 UTC]     15B v0001 PUT doc.txt (latest)

$ nexoctl retention clear --default mem/vault
Removed the default retention of `mem/vault`.

$ nexoctl retention info mem/vault
`mem/vault` has Object Lock, without default retention.

$ nexoctl retention set --mode governance mem/vault/doc.txt
! nexoctl: error: --mode and --validity are required
! Run 'nexoctl retention set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl retention set --mode forever --validity 1d mem/vault/doc.txt
! nexoctl: error: invalid --mode "forever" (governance, compliance)
! Run 'nexoctl retention set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl retention set --mode governance --validity 3w mem/vault/doc.txt
! nexoctl: error: invalid validity "3w": the unit is d (days) or y (years)
! Run 'nexoctl retention set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl retention set --mode governance --validity 1d mem/vault
! nexoctl: error: mem/vault is a bucket: use --default for its default retention or --recursive for its objects
! Run 'nexoctl retention set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl retention set --default --bypass --mode governance --validity 1d mem/vault
! nexoctl: error: --default sets the default retention of a bucket: it excludes --bypass, --version-id, --recursive and --versions
! Run 'nexoctl retention set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl legalhold set mem/vault
! nexoctl: error: mem/vault is a bucket: use --recursive for its objects
! Run 'nexoctl legalhold set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl legalhold set --version-id v1 -r mem/vault/
! nexoctl: error: mem/vault: --version-id selects one version: it excludes --recursive and --versions
! Run 'nexoctl legalhold set --help' for usage.
[exit 2]

$ nexoctl legalhold info mem/plain/missing
! nexoctl: error: mem/plain/missing: invalid argument: bucket plain is missing Object Lock configuration (InvalidRequest)
[exit 1]

